li.t:
when record_type is not padding, the leaf is of a type this document
does not define (finding non_record_leaf_type_unsupported), and the
verifier checks nothing further about it;

when the padding content does not have exactly the four members above,
each in the form above, with epistemic_type equal to producer_claim,
it is malformed (finding non_record_leaf_malformed);

section.artwork:
"category_coverage": {
  "set": "<category set identifier>",
  "categories": {
    "<category name>": { "status": "AVAILABLE" },
    "<category name>": { "status": "UNDISCLOSED",
                         "policy_uri": "<absolute URI>" }
  },
  "request_digest": "<64 hex>",
  "signer": { "key_id": "<64 hex>" },
  "signature": "<128 hex>"
}

dd.t:
NOT_CHECKED when the verifier does not have the Evidence Request;
otherwise FAIL when request_digest is present and is not that
request's digest, computed over its octets before they are parsed;
otherwise NOT_CHECKED when the request cannot be read, or its
categories field is malformed ();
NOT_PRESENT when the request has no categories field; FAIL when the
request names another set, or a requested category has no entry; PASS
otherwise.

section.artwork:
"extensions": {
  "composed/v1": {
    "members": [
      { "id": "<member id>", "observer": "<observer id>",
        "request_digest": "<64 hex>", "outcome": "artifact",
        "digest": "<64 hex>", "bundle": { ... } },
      { "id": "<member id>", "observer": "<observer id>",
        "request_digest": "<64 hex>", "outcome": "refusal",
        "digest": "<64 hex>", "refusal": { ... } }
    ],
    "observers": [
      { "id": "<observer id>", "role": "<role>",
        "custody_domain": "<label>" }
    ],
    "joins": [
      { "members": ["<member id>", "<member id>"],
        "basis": "pre_agreed_identifier",
        "pointer": "<JSON Pointer>",
        "identifier_digest": "<64 hex>",
        "compare": ["<JSON Pointer>"],
        "state": "agree" }
    ],
    "not_requested": [ "<participant id>" ],
    "missing": [ "<member id>" ],
    "composed_digest": "<64 hex>"
  }
}

section.sourcecode:
composed-v1 = { members: [+ composed-member], observers: [+ composed-observer], ? joins: [* composed-join], ? not_requested: [* label-id], ? missing: [* label-id], composed_digest: digest-hex, }
composed-member = artifact-member / refusal-member / absence-member
member-common = ( id: label-id, observer: label-id, ; an observers[].id request_digest: digest-hex, ; the Evidence Request this answers digest: digest-hex, ; see "Members and Outcomes" )
artifact-member = { member-common, outcome: "artifact", ? bundle: { * tstr => any }, ; a Bundle ? response: artifact-response } refusal-member = { member-common, outcome: "refusal", ? refusal: signed-refusal } absence-member = { member-common, outcome: "absence", ? absence: recorded-absence }
signed-refusal = { ; as received, unmodified request_digest: digest-hex, reason: tstr, ; Evidence Request refusal reason issued_at: tstr, ; RFC 3339 * tstr => any, ; deployment signature members }
artifact-response = { ; as received, minus artifact bytes request_digest: digest-hex, artifact_digest: digest-hex, * tstr => any, ; deployment members and signature }
recorded-absence = { ; the requester's own record request_digest: digest-hex, window: { from: tstr, to: tstr }, ; RFC 3339 ? route: tstr, ? commitment: digest-hex, ; a retention commitment it held }
composed-observer = { id: label-id, role: tstr, ; see "Observers and Redundancy" custody_domain: tstr, ; opaque, compared octet-for-octet }
composed-join = { members: [label-id, label-id], ; two distinct ids, ascending basis: join-basis, ? pointer: tstr, ; RFC 6901 JSON Pointer ? identifier_digest: digest-hex, ? compare: [+ tstr], ; RFC 6901 JSON Pointers state: join-state, }
join-basis = "pre_agreed_identifier" / "shared_artifact_digest" / "issued_receipt" / "same_interval" / "controller_binding" join-state = "agree" / "mismatch" / "unjoined" / "one_sided"
label-id = text .regexp "[A-Za-z0-9._:-]{1,128}" digest-hex = text .regexp "[0-9a-f]{64}"

controller-binding = { binding_version: "controller-binding/0", claim: binding-claim, method: tstr, ; a verification method token keys: [key-id, key-id], ; two distinct keys, ascending issued_at: binding-time, ; the ceremony, as stated not_before: binding-time, ; not later than issued_at not_after: binding-time, ; later than issued_at revocation: "revocation_statement/0", nonce: tstr, ; non-empty, chosen per ceremony sigs: [* binding-sig], ? key_types: [tstr, tstr], ; one per entry of keys, in order ? delegator: key-id, ; delegated_by only: one of keys ? credential: binding-credential, ; same_organization_credentialed }
binding-claim = "same_controller_asserted" / "delegated_by" / "same_organization_credentialed" binding-sig = { key_id: key-id, sig: any } ; sig-hex for ed25519 binding-credential = { issuer: key-id, method: tstr, digest: digest-hex, }
binding-revocation = { revocation_version: "controller-binding-revocation/0", binding: digest-hex, ; the binding digest key_id: key-id, ; one of the binding's keys revoked_at: binding-time, sig: sig-hex, }
key-id = text .regexp "[0-9a-f]{64}" sig-hex = text .regexp "[0-9a-f]{128}" binding-time = text .regexp "[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}T[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}Z"

li.t:
same_organization_credentialed: adds credential;
dual_signature_credential/0. Both keys are held within one organization,
as a credential from a third key states.

section.artwork:
{
  "type": "countersign/v1",
  "signer": { "id": "<signer identifier>", "key_id": "<64 hex>" },
  "over": "<bundle digest>",
  "statement": {
    "checks": [ {"name": "<check>", "result": "<result>"}, ... ],
    "recomputed_at": "<RFC 3339 UTC timestamp>",
    "scope": {
      "ledger_id": "<ledger identifier>",
      "period": { "from": "<RFC 3339>", "to": "<RFC 3339>" },
      "closure_depth": 2
    }
  },
  "signature": "<128 hex>",
  "receipt": { ... }
}

li.t:
recompute the bundle digest and compare it to over. An entry whose over
differs is not a countersignature of this Bundle and MUST be reported as
invalid;

verify signature over the signing input under signer.key_id. An entry
whose signature fails is invalid, and its checks MUST NOT be displayed as
results;
